<title>Activity Synthesis</title>
<para>Invite students to share their answers and the methods they used to solve each rectangle. </para>
<para><emphasis>Use the following questions to lead a class discussion.</emphasis></para>
<list type="enumerated">
  <item> How did you find the length when given the width and area? (Possible answer: multiply) </item>
  <item> How did you find the length and width given the area? (Possible answer: factor) </item>
  <item> Which rectangles represent perfect square trinomials? (Possible answers: C, G, I) </item>
  <item> Which rectangles represent the difference of squares? (Possible answers: B, F, K) </item>
  <item> Which rectangle(s) required grouping? (Possible answer: L) </item>
</list></section>
